{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To solve the problem, we first need to understand the function \\( f(x) = x - \\lfloor \\sqrt{x} \\rfloor^2 \\). The function \\( f(x) \\) gives the difference between \\( x \\) and the square of the greatest integer less than or equal to the square root of \\( x \\).\n\nLet's evaluate \\( f(x) \\) for each integer \\( x \\) from 101 to 110.\n\n1. For \\( x = 101 \\):\n   \\[\n   \\lfloor \\sqrt{101} \\rfloor = 10 \\quad \\text{(since } 10^2 = 100 \\text{ and } 11^2 = 121\\text{)}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   f(101) = 101 - 10^2 = 101 - 100 = 1\n   \\]\n\n2. For \\( x = 102 \\):\n   \\[\n   \\lfloor \\sqrt{102} \\rfloor = 10\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   f(102) = 102 - 10^2 = 102 - 100 = 2\n   \\]\n\n3. For \\( x = 103 \\):\n   \\[\n   \\lfloor \\sqrt{103} \\rfloor = 10\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   f(103) = 103 - 10^2 = 103 - 100 = 3\n   \\]\n\n4. For \\( x = 104 \\):\n   \\[\n   \\lfloor \\sqrt{104} \\rfloor = 10\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   f(104) = 104 - 10^2 = 104 - 100 = 4\n   \\]\n\n5. For \\( x = 105 \\):\n   \\[\n   \\lfloor \\sqrt{105} \\rfloor = 10\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   f(105) = 105 - 10^2 = 105 - 100 = 5\n   \\]\n\n","prefix_end":997,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":false,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,11625,279,3491,11,582,1156,1184,311,3535,279,729,17767,282,2075,8,284,856,481,1124,11008,3993,1124,26888,45340,92,1124,8052,3993,61,17,1124,568,576,729,17767,282,2075,8,1124,8,6696,279,6672,1948,17767,856,1124,8,323,279,9334,315,279,12196,7546,2686,1091,476,6144,311,279,9334,3704,315,17767,856,1124,3593,10061,594,15442,17767,282,2075,8,1124,8,369,1817,7546,17767,856,1124,8,504,220,16,15,16,311,220,16,16,15,382,16,13,1752,17767,856,284,220,16,15,16,1124,982,256,1124,9640,256,1124,11008,3993,1124,26888,90,16,15,16,92,1124,8052,3993,284,220,16,15,1124,31610,1124,1318,96065,11284,335,220,16,15,61,17,284,220,16,15,15,1124,1318,90,323,335,220,16,16,61,17,284,220,16,17,16,59,13